# Toy RNAs for explaining CoSTAR. Made up for illustration; not real molecules.
# Format: ">name", then the sequence, then the structure (dot-bracket).
#   "(" pairs with its ")", "[" pairs with its "]", "." is unpaired.
#
# A: two crossing stems (an H-type pseudoknot)
# B: like A, but the first stem has one extra pair, plus an extra hairpin at the 3' end
# C: the first stem and the hairpin, but no crossing partner
>A
GGGGAAAAGCGCAAAACCCCAAAAGCGC
((((....[[[[....))))....]]]]
>B
GGGGGAAAAGCGCAAAACCCCCAAAAGCGCAAGAGAAAAAUCUC
(((((....[[[[....)))))....]]]]..((((....))))
>C
GGGGAAAAAAAAAAAACCCCAAGAGAAAAAUCUC
((((............))))..((((....))))
